# WordPress / EMCP Safety Rules

This WordPress installation is managed through the EMCP MCP server.

## General safety

- Use EMCP MCP tools for WordPress and Elementor changes.
- Inspect before modifying.
- Never guess the current page structure.
- Before modifying an existing Elementor page, inspect its structure first.
- Before modifying an existing widget, inspect its current settings first.
- Never invoke destructive tools unless the user explicitly requests the destructive action.
- Never delete pages, templates, media, products, users or settings without explicit user approval.
- Never use direct database writes.
- Never use filesystem writes.
- Never use WP-CLI.
- Never install, update, deactivate or remove plugins or themes unless explicitly requested.
- Never create or activate PHP snippets unless explicitly requested.
- Never modify WordPress core files.

## Publishing

New pages and templates must be created as drafts first.

Do not publish:
- pages
- headers
- footers
- Theme Builder templates
- WooCommerce templates

until they have passed visual QA or the user explicitly requests publication.

## Elementor discovery

Never invent Elementor control names.

Before using an unfamiliar widget:
1. Discover the available widget.
2. Read its schema.
3. Use only controls returned by the schema.

If an Elementor setting appears not to work, inspect the schema instead of guessing alternative setting names.

## Minimal change principle

When correcting an existing page:
- update only the affected elements;
- do not regenerate the entire page unless specifically requested;
- preserve unrelated content and settings.

## Code

Prefer native Elementor functionality.

Priority:
1. Elementor Core
2. Elementor Pro
3. WooCommerce widgets
4. Existing approved plugins
5. Custom CSS
6. Custom HTML/JavaScript

Custom code is a last resort.

## WooCommerce

WooCommerce read operations are permitted.

Do not create, update or delete:
- products
- orders
- customers
- coupons
- tax rules
- payment settings
- shipping settings

unless explicitly instructed.